# link.nagarva.in
#
# THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO CATCH-ALL HERE.
#
# The 17 Aug 2026 incident was caused by exactly one line:
#     /*    /index.html   200
# combined with the /auth relay page sitting at the site root. That made
# EVERY path — /survey, /sign, /quote, /track — serve "Email confirmed —
# your Nagarva account is ready" to customers who had clicked a survey or
# signature link. Worse than a 404: it reads as a broken or phishing link
# sent by their own mover.
#
# Every path here is a real directory with a real index.html, so Netlify
# serves the file directly and never consults this file. Unknown paths
# fall through to 404.html, which is the honest answer.
#
# If you add an SPA later, scope its rewrite to that app's own prefix.
# Never re-add a site-wide /* rule.
